  "scenes": [
    {
      "narration": "A million dollars means something completely different depending on where you spend it. Let's rank where it still makes you rich.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "hook",
          "art": "globe",
          "props": [
            "coin",
            "globe"
          ],
          "lines": [
            "Where $1M",
            "is still rich."
          ]
        }
      ],
      "id": "s1"
    },
    {
      "narration": "The gap is enormous. A million lasts about fifteen years in the priciest country and ninety in the cheapest.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "stat",
          "art": "globe",
          "big": "15 vs 90 yrs",
          "label": "how long $1M lasts",
          "props": [
            "clock",
            "coin"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "id": "s2"
    },
    {
      "narration": "It all comes down to purchasing power, what the money actually buys.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "evidence",
          "sourceId": "wiki-ppower",
          "kicker": "Wikipedia · purchasing power"
        }
      ],
      "id": "s3"
    },
    {
      "narration": "Carry that same million to a low-cost country, and it can feel like three or four million of real life.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "stat",
          "art": "globe",
          "big": "$1M → $3–4M",
          "label": "of real life, abroad",
          "props": [
            "coin",
            "check"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "id": "s4"
    },
    {
      "narration": "In a cheap country, a million can mean full financial independence.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "evidence",
          "sourceId": "wiki-fi",
          "kicker": "Wikipedia · financial independence"
        }
      ],
      "id": "s5"
    },
    {
      "narration": "In an expensive city, though, a million barely buys a modest home and a cautious retirement.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "stat",
          "art": "home",
          "big": "a house",
          "label": "all $1M buys in pricey cities",
          "props": [
            "home",
            "x"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "id": "s6"
    },
    {
      "narration": "The word millionaire hasn't meant truly rich for a long time.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "evidence",
          "sourceId": "wiki-millionaire",
          "kicker": "Wikipedia · millionaire"
        }
      ],
      "id": "s7"
    },
    {
      "narration": "The word millionaire is really just a passport to a very different cost of living.",
